Not a real file to add as-is — this is a diff note for a small addition to
the upstream file netwerk/base/nsNetUtil.cpp (verified present at this path
in the pinned tree, target/gecko-src/gecko-dev/, at the live-tested commit
5836a062726f715fda621338a17b51aff30d0a8c on branch central-work).

## Why this file is touched at all

This is a genuine stock-file change, not a netwerk/protocol/pyxis/-local
one — flagged explicitly per the project's "prefer components.conf-only
fixes" discipline, because no components.conf-only fix exists for this bug.
See BUILD_RUNBOOK.md's dated entry ("isSecureContext / null principal root
cause") for the full investigation. Summary: `NS_NewURI` in this file picks
the concrete C++ nsIURI implementation class via a hardcoded, scheme-by-
scheme if/else chain — it does NOT consult the registered nsIProtocolHandler
flags (components.conf's `protocol_config.flags`) to make that choice.
`URI_STD` (value 0 in nsIProtocolHandler.idl) is documentary only. A scheme
absent from this chain falls through to the `network.url.useDefaultURI`
branch and gets a `DefaultURI` instance (netwerk/base/DefaultURI.h), which
implements only nsIURI/nsISerializable/nsISizeOf — NOT nsIStandardURL.

That silently broke pyxis:// content-principal creation end-to-end:
`ContentPrincipal::GenerateOriginNoSuffixFromURI` (caps/ContentPrincipal.cpp)
does a `do_QueryInterface` to nsIStandardURL and returns NS_ERROR_FAILURE if
that fails, and `BasePrincipal::CreateContentPrincipal(nsIURI*, ...)`
(caps/BasePrincipal.cpp) silently maps that failure to `NullPrincipal::
Create()` — no error surfaced anywhere. This is exactly what was live-tested
and observed: page content loaded correctly (registration/origin-resolution/
path-confinement/serving all genuinely work), but
`gBrowser.selectedBrowser.contentPrincipal.originNoSuffix` read
"moz-nullprincipal:{uuid}" instead of "pyxis://testapp", and
`window.isSecureContext` read false as a direct, correct consequence of
having a null principal (null principals are never secure contexts,
independent of the URI's own registered URI_IS_POTENTIALLY_TRUSTWORTHY flag,
which IS correctly registered and IS correctly readable via
URIChainHasFlags — that part was never the bug).

moz-extension: avoids this failure mode because its hardcoded NS_NewURI case
(a few lines below this insertion point) calls
`ExtensionProtocolHandler::NewURI`, which is a `SubstitutingProtocolHandler`
whose URI type, `SubstitutingURL` (netwerk/protocol/res/
SubstitutingProtocolHandler.cpp), literally subclasses `nsStandardURL`.
pyxis:// doesn't need moz-extension:'s substitution/resolution logic — it
just needs to be constructed as a plain `nsStandardURL` instance, same as
the existing indexeddb:/uuid: case immediately above the insertion point
uses.

## The change

Insert a new scheme case in `NS_NewURI(nsIURI** aURI, const nsACString&
aSpec, const char* aCharset, nsIURI* aBaseURI)`, immediately after the
existing `indexeddb`/`uuid` case and immediately before the existing
`moz-extension` case (all three are in the same hardcoded if/else chain).
Exact insertion point — the existing code immediately before and after,
unchanged, for anchoring:

    if (scheme.EqualsLiteral("indexeddb") || scheme.EqualsLiteral("uuid")) {
      return NS_MutateURI(new nsStandardURL::Mutator())
          .Apply(&nsIStandardURLMutator::Init, nsIStandardURL::URLTYPE_AUTHORITY,
                 0, aSpec, aCharset, aBaseURI, nullptr)
          .Finalize(aURI);
    }

    // <-- NEW CODE INSERTED HERE, see below -->

    if (scheme.EqualsLiteral("moz-extension")) {
      RefPtr<mozilla::net::ExtensionProtocolHandler> handler =
          mozilla::net::ExtensionProtocolHandler::GetSingleton();
      if (!handler) {
        return NS_ERROR_NOT_AVAILABLE;
      }
      return handler->NewURI(aSpec, aCharset, aBaseURI, aURI);
    }

New code inserted at that point (see this directory's sibling file
netwerk/protocol/pyxis/PyxisProtocolHandler.h for the point-5 SCAFFOLD
NOTICE correction that explains, in the handler's own docs, why this was
needed despite the handler having no custom NewURI override):

    // Pyxis (GeckoOS): pyxis://<app-id>/<path> app-serving scheme. Registered
    // with URI_STD in netwerk/protocol/pyxis/components.conf, but that flag
    // alone only affects nsIProtocolHandler flag queries (URIChainHasFlags) --
    // it does NOT influence which concrete nsIURI class gets instantiated here.
    // Unless a scheme is one of the hardcoded cases in this function, unknown
    // schemes fall through to DefaultURI (see the network.url.useDefaultURI
    // branch below), which does not implement nsIStandardURL. That silently
    // broke content-principal creation: ContentPrincipal::
    // GenerateOriginNoSuffixFromURI (caps/ContentPrincipal.cpp) requires a
    // do_QueryInterface to nsIStandardURL and fails closed (NS_ERROR_FAILURE)
    // otherwise, which BasePrincipal::CreateContentPrincipal (caps/
    // BasePrincipal.cpp) silently maps to a NullPrincipal -- reproducing the
    // observed bug (window.isSecureContext false, contentPrincipal a
    // moz-nullprincipal: instead of pyxis://<app-id>). moz-extension: avoids
    // this via its own hardcoded case below, whose SubstitutingURL literally
    // subclasses nsStandardURL. pyxis:// doesn't need substitution/resolution,
    // just a real nsIStandardURL instance, so route it through the same
    // nsStandardURL + URLTYPE_AUTHORITY construction used for indexeddb/uuid
    // above (default_port -1 matches this scheme's components.conf entry).
    if (scheme.EqualsLiteral("pyxis")) {
      return NS_MutateURI(new nsStandardURL::Mutator())
          .Apply(&nsIStandardURLMutator::Init, nsIStandardURL::URLTYPE_AUTHORITY,
                 -1, aSpec, aCharset, aBaseURI, nullptr)
          .Finalize(aURI);
    }

This has been applied to the live checkout at
target/gecko-src/gecko-dev/netwerk/base/nsNetUtil.cpp (this mirror is a
diff-note, not a full-file copy, matching the convention already used for
toolkit/actors/ActorManagerParent.sys.mjs.PYXIS_DIFF in this same patch
series — nsNetUtil.cpp is a large (~4200 line) stock file we don't own, so
we track the delta here rather than a full duplicate).

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
The unified diff below is generated from the checkout and is applied with
  git apply gecko/patches/pyxis/<path>.PYXIS_DIFF
(or `patch -p1 <`). Everything above this line is rationale, not content;
git apply ignores it. Regenerate with scripts/regen-gecko-patches.sh.
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

diff --git a/netwerk/base/nsNetUtil.cpp b/netwerk/base/nsNetUtil.cpp
index 2074d7e305f2..759ad6b84812 100644
--- a/netwerk/base/nsNetUtil.cpp
+++ b/netwerk/base/nsNetUtil.cpp
@@ -1966,6 +1966,32 @@ nsresult NS_NewURI(nsIURI** aURI, const nsACString& aSpec,
         .Finalize(aURI);
   }
 
+  // Pyxis (GeckoOS): pyxis://<app-id>/<path> app-serving scheme. Registered
+  // with URI_STD in netwerk/protocol/pyxis/components.conf, but that flag
+  // alone only affects nsIProtocolHandler flag queries (URIChainHasFlags) --
+  // it does NOT influence which concrete nsIURI class gets instantiated here.
+  // Unless a scheme is one of the hardcoded cases in this function, unknown
+  // schemes fall through to DefaultURI (see the network.url.useDefaultURI
+  // branch below), which does not implement nsIStandardURL. That silently
+  // broke content-principal creation: ContentPrincipal::
+  // GenerateOriginNoSuffixFromURI (caps/ContentPrincipal.cpp) requires a
+  // do_QueryInterface to nsIStandardURL and fails closed (NS_ERROR_FAILURE)
+  // otherwise, which BasePrincipal::CreateContentPrincipal (caps/
+  // BasePrincipal.cpp) silently maps to a NullPrincipal -- reproducing the
+  // observed bug (window.isSecureContext false, contentPrincipal a
+  // moz-nullprincipal: instead of pyxis://<app-id>). moz-extension: avoids
+  // this via its own hardcoded case below, whose SubstitutingURL literally
+  // subclasses nsStandardURL. pyxis:// doesn't need substitution/resolution,
+  // just a real nsIStandardURL instance, so route it through the same
+  // nsStandardURL + URLTYPE_AUTHORITY construction used for indexeddb/uuid
+  // above (default_port -1 matches this scheme's components.conf entry).
+  if (scheme.EqualsLiteral("pyxis")) {
+    return NS_MutateURI(new nsStandardURL::Mutator())
+        .Apply(&nsIStandardURLMutator::Init, nsIStandardURL::URLTYPE_AUTHORITY,
+               -1, aSpec, aCharset, aBaseURI, nullptr)
+        .Finalize(aURI);
+  }
+
   if (scheme.EqualsLiteral("moz-extension")) {
     RefPtr<mozilla::net::ExtensionProtocolHandler> handler =
         mozilla::net::ExtensionProtocolHandler::GetSingleton();
